  "name": "Diversity and Criminal Justice in Canada",
  "description": "This course focuses on the practical implications of cultural diversity for criminal justice professionals. The course examines multiculturalism, Indigenous histories and perspectives, and the impacts of systemic bias on decision-making within policing, courts, and corrections. Students learn strategies for culturally responsive and trauma-informed practice, effective communication, and ethical engagement with diverse communities. Emphasis is placed on developing professional competencies that support fairness, accountability, and public trust in the criminal justice system",
